From d681172827499f10ca05769e9776933431fe9f84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:26:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/58] dsv4 indexer: publish prefill candidate masks at block
 granularity (E34b-ii)

select_candidate_block_keep returns the [rows, ceil(width/block_size)] keep mask;
expand_candidate_blocks is the old repeat_interleave(block_size)[..., :width].
select_candidate_blocks (decode) is the composition, unchanged in output.
Both prefill paths (_dense_index_topk_rows, _low_ratio_index_topk_torch) publish
the block form and expand only the consumer's own row tile. The per-position
mask was 1 GiB per 4096-row chunk at 262K prefix and, doubled by torch.cat,
the OOM at 184K (recipe E34b). Consumers assert the published block count
matches their lc.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
---
